      examples: ['A questionnaire on a sensitive topic may produce socially desirable answers, reducing validity.', 'A school gatekeeper may only permit access to one year group, limiting representativeness.', 'Triangulation can combine methods to strengthen understanding.'],
      compare: ['Positivists tend to value measurement, reliability and patterns; interpretivists tend to prioritise meaning and validity.', 'No method is simply “best”. Suitability depends on the question.', 'Practical problems and methodological weaknesses are related but not identical.'],
      mistakes: ['Do not define methods without applying them to the proposed research.', 'Do not say “large sample = representative” automatically.', 'Do not name an ethical issue without explaining how it arises in this study.'],
